#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktts; is a subsysem within &kde; for producing Text-to-Speech (TTS). It "
"provides a common API for &kde; programmers to give TTS capabilities to "
"their applications. It provides some nice capabilities for end users as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "User features:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak contents of a text file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak &kde; notification events (KNotify)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak all or part of the text of a web page in &konqueror;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Speak all or part of the text in &kate; text editor, including instances "
"where &kate; is embedded in another &kde; application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Speech is spoken via speech-dispatcher, so any speech-dispatcher backend can "
"be used (espeak, festival, &etc;)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"User-configurable filters for substituting misspoken words, choosing speech "
"synthesizers, and transforming XHMTL/&XML; documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Programmer features:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Priority system for screen reader outputs, warnings and messages, while "
"still playing regular texts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Permit generation of speech from the command line (or via shell scripts) "
"using the &qdbus; utility."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Provide a lightweight and easily usable interface for applications to "
"generate speech output."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applications need not be concerned about contention over the speech device."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"FUTURE: Provide support for speech markup languages, such as VoiceXML, "
"Sable, &Java; Speech Markup Language (JSML), and Speech Markup Meta-language "
"(SMML)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "FUTURE: Provide limited support for embedded speech markers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Asynchronous to prevent system blocking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ktts; actually consists of several programs:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kttsd</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the &kde; Text-to-Speech Daemon, which is a non-&GUI; application that "
"provides TTS services to applications via &DBus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kttsmgr</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"a &GUI; application for configuring and controlling kttsd. kttsmgr sits in "
"the system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "libkhtmlkttsdplugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A plugin for the &konqueror; web browser that permits you to speak all or a "
"portion of the text on a web page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "ktexteditor_kttsd"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A plugin for the &kate; text editor that permits you to speak all or a "
"portion of a text file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Support"
msgstr "Ajuda"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to the &kde; Bugzilla database ( <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde."
"org/\">http://bugs.kde.org/</ulink> ), discussions for &ktts; currently take "
"place in the kde-accessibility mailing list. Subscribe at <ulink url="
"\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-accessibility\"> https://mail."
"kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kde-accessibility</ulink>. Developers also hang out "
"in IRC (irc.kde.org, channel #kde-accessibility)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &ktts;"
msgstr "Utilizr &ktts;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you can use &ktts;, you must install speech-dispatcher and make sure "
"it is working. See <xref linkend=\"installation\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting <command>kttsmgr</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "To start the &ktts; system, type the following command in a &konsole;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>kttsmgr</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "or click on kttsmgr in the &kde; Menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is the first time running <command>kttsmgr</command>, or if you have "
"not yet configured any talkers, the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> screen "
"appears. See <xref linkend=\"configure-talkers\"/>. If you have already "
"configured at least one talker, the <guilabel>General</guilabel> screen "
"appears. See <xref linkend=\"general\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:273
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Configuration"
msgid "Configuring Talkers"
msgstr "Configuracion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most text-to-speech (TTS) synthesizers offer multiple languages and voices "
"and may offer multiple speaking genders, volumes, and rates. You may "
"configure more than one instance of a synthesizer. Each combination of "
"language, synthesizer, voice, gender, volume, and rate is called a talker. "
"You should configure at least one talker before you use &ktts; otherwise "
"speech-dispatcher will use a default voice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multiple talkers for the same synthesizer is similar to multiple print "
"queues for a single physical printer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> tab in <command>kttsmgr</"
"command>, the <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> screen appears. This screen also "
"automatically appears if you start <command>kttsmgr</command> and you have "
"not yet configured any talkers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Talkers tab)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (Talkers tab)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click to add a new talker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the configured <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> are listed here. Highest "
"priority <guilabel>Talkers</guilabel> are listed at the top. The top-most "
"talker will be used to do the speaking when an application does not specify "
"a talker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on a talker in the list to highlight it and click this button to "
"remove it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on a talker in the list to highlight it and click this button to "
"change its configuration. See below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on a talker in the list to highlight it and click this button to move "
"it down one row in the list. The lower a talker appears in the list, the "
"lower its priority."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click one of these buttons to apply the changes you have made to the running "
"&ktts; system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> button, the <guilabel>Add "
"Talker</guilabel> screen appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Talker screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Talker screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "You should give your new talker a name, this can be anything."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose the language and synthesizer here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the voice type here, there are three Male, three Female, one Male "
"Child and one Female Child voices to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set any custom voice parameters here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
