#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are almost ready to begin using &ktts;. Now go back to the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> tab and check the <guilabel>Enable Text-to-"
"Speech System (KTTSD)</guilabel> box. This will start the &kde; TTS Daemon. "
"See <xref linkend=\"general\"/>. You may now begin using &ktts; to speak "
"text. Click the <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> tab to create and manage text "
"jobs. See <xref linkend=\"jobmgr\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting KTTSD and Setting General Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have configured at least one talker, you can start the &kde; Text-"
"to-Speech System. Click on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab. The "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> screen appears. You can also set some general "
"options on this screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (General tab)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Text-to-Speech Manager (General tab)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this box to activate the &ktts; system. This starts the &kde; TTS "
"Daemon (KTTSD). If KTTSD starts successfully, the <guilabel>Jobs</guilabel> "
"tab will appear. Once KTTSD has been started, you can begin creating and "
"speaking text jobs. See <xref linkend=\"jobmgr\"/>. Unchecking will stop "
"KTTSD and deactivate the &kde; TTS system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this box is checked, an icon appears in the system tray whenever "
"<command>kttsmgr</command> is running. In this mode, clicking <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> or <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> does not cause <command>kttsmgr</"
"command> to exit. Instead, the screen disappears but <command>kttsmgr</"
"command> continues running in the system tray. Click the icon to restore the "
"screen. To quit <command>kttsmgr</command>, right-click on the icon in the "
"system tray and choose <guilabel>Quit</guilabel>. When unchecked, an icon "
"does not appear in the system tray. Clicking <guibutton>OK</guibutton> or "
"<guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> quits <command>kttsmgr</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When <command>kttsmgr</command> exits, &ktts; keeps running if the "
"<guilabel>Enable Text-to-Speech System (KTTSD)</guilabel> box is checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option does not take effect until the next time <command>kttsmgr</"
"command> is started."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option has no effect when <command>kttsmgr</command> is running in the "
"&kcontrol;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this box is checked, and <command>kttsmgr</command> automatically "
"appears in the system tray whenever speaking, it will also disappear "
"automatically when speaking has finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Be sure to click here to save your settings."
msgstr ""

